2026\/04\/tensor-flow.webp 633w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/tensor-flow-300x197.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 633px) 100vw, 633px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.tensorflow.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">TensorFlow<\/a> is a powerful open-source framework widely used for machine learning and deep learning in data science. Developed by Google, it helps users build, train, and deploy neural networks and AI models efficiently. It is commonly used for image recognition, natural language processing, and predictive analytics.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h5 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Use TensorFlow for Data Science?<\/h5>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Deep Learning Support:<\/strong> Ideal for building neural networks and complex AI models.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Scalable Framework:<\/strong> Works efficiently for both small projects and large-scale applications.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Model Deployment:<\/strong> Supports easy deployment on web, mobile, and cloud platforms.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>GPU and TPU Support:<\/strong> Speeds up training for large datasets and deep learning tasks.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Strong Community:<\/strong> Backed by extensive documentation and a large developer community.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">12. PyTorch<\/h4>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1890\" height=\"1074\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/pytorch.webp\" alt=\"PyTorch\" class=\"wp-image-18087\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1.7597957379946971;width:386px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/pytorch.webp 1890w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/pytorch-300x170.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/pytorch-1024x582.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/pytorch-768x436.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/pytorch-1536x873.webp 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1890px) 100vw, 1890px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/pytorch.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">PyTorch<\/a> is a commonly used open-source deep learning framework in data science and artificial intelligence. Developed by Meta Platforms, it is known for its flexibility, dynamic computation graph, and ease of use. It is commonly used for building neural networks, research projects, computer vision, and natural language processing applications.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h5 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Use PyTorch for Data Science?<\/h5>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Deep Learning Framework:<\/strong> Ideal for building and training neural networks.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Dynamic Computation Graph:<\/strong> Allows you to modify models during runtime, making it easier to experiment and debug.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Research Friendly:<\/strong> Widely preferred for AI research and experimentation.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>GPU Support:<\/strong> Speeds up model training with efficient hardware acceleration.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Python Based:<\/strong> Simple syntax and strong integration with Python libraries.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">13. Keras<\/h4>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1000\" height=\"655\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/keras.webp\" alt=\"Keras\" class=\"wp-image-18089\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1.6650554449815183;width:403px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/keras.webp 1000w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blo